-- Document-level constraints of the Resolved Deployment, asked of a resolution
-- before anything is rendered from it (docs/adr/emf/0143). Each invariant is
-- named after the diagnostic code it reports, and its feature is the position
-- the refusal is written at in the project file the Process comes from.

import 'https://jorisjonkers.dev/deploy-kit/resolved-deployment/1'

package resolveddeployment

context ResolvedProcess
	-- Every dimension a Process declared is matched against the node contract, so
	-- no eligible node is a Process nothing can hold: its replicas, a writable path
	-- held in memory, the seeder beside it and the pool its L4 Addresses hold it to
	-- all count (spec/v1/20-resolved-deployment.md#layer-2-does-not-assign-a-node).
	inv E_PLACEMENT_UNSATISFIABLE__placement:
		placement.eligibleNodes->notEmpty()

	-- Replicas spread across nodes need a node each, and a rollout's old and new
	-- pod may still share one, so fewer eligible nodes than the count leaves a
	-- replica that never schedules. None eligible is the placement's own refusal.
	inv E_PLACEMENT_UNSATISFIABLE__replicas:
		(spread and placement.eligibleNodes->notEmpty())
			implies placement.eligibleNodes->size() >= replicas

endpackage
